Feature: artie generate --format yaml, with reason steps kept and the run in words
  spec/PLAN-KEPT-SCRIPTS-AS-DATA.md, step 3. As generate-options.feature, for
  a script held as data. With --keep-reason, a step where the reasoner chose
  a value stays its words, marked reasoned: true, for the model on every run.
  With --intents, the script is the intent rung, kind: intent: every act and
  follow its words alone, the run's shape kept (its nesting, reads, waits and
  checks); a goal run's watch too, from the watch as data its capture keeps.

  Background:
    Given the file "run.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs:
          owner:
            value: acme
            given: given
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      line: 1
      params:
        entry: http://localhost:8392/
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open the repository acme
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params:
        relation: repos-get
        owner: acme
      values:
        owner:
          value: acme
          from:
            - input: owner
      reason:
        template: open the repository $owner
        slots:
          owner:
            value: acme
            from:
              - input: owner
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
      line: 3
      within: 2
      params:
        relation: open-issue
        title: Crash on start
        body: Opened by a script.
      values:
        title:
          value: Crash on start
          from:
            - words
        body:
          value: Opened by a script.
          from:
            - paraphrase
      reason:
        template: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
        slots: {}
      opens: true
      outcome: new resource
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: 'comment on it: Thanks.'
      line: 4
      within: 3
      params:
        relation: comment
        body: Thanks.
      values:
        body:
          value: Thanks.
          from:
            - words
      reason:
        template: 'comment on it: Thanks.'
        slots: {}
      opens: true
      outcome: new resource
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: close it, since it's done
      line: 5
      within: 3
      params:
        relation: close
        reason: completed
      values:
        reason:
          value: completed
          from:
            - chosen
      reason:
        template: close it, since it's done
        slots: {}
      outcome: done
      """

  Scenario: --keep-reason keeps a step whose value the reasoner chose as its words, marked reasoned
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.heart.yaml |
      | --keep-reason  |
      | --format       |
      | yaml           |
    Then artie exits 0
    And artie prints
      | line                                                         |
      | wrote gen.heart.yaml: 0 values to review, 1 reason step kept |
      | wrote gen.pins.yaml: 0 forms and 0 links pinned              |
    And the file "gen.heart.yaml" reads
      """yaml
      # Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      # Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested; where the reasoner chose a value, its reason step is kept.
      # What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      # 1 step calls the model on every run: artie run needs --reasoner.
      #   artie run gen.heart.yaml owner=acme --reasoner claude
      heart: 1
      kind: kept
      start: http://localhost:8392/

      inputs:
        owner:

      steps:
        - act: repos-get
          fields:
            owner: ${owner}
          intent: open the repository ${owner}
          then:
            - act: open-issue
              fields:
                title: Crash on start
                body: Opened by a script.
              intent: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
              then:
                - sync: true
                - act: comment
                  fields:
                    body: Thanks.
                  intent: "comment on it: Thanks."
                  then: []
                - intent: close it, since it's done
                  reasoned: true
      """
    And the file "gen.heart.yaml" is a script as data, by spec/schemas/heart-script.draft.schema.json

  Scenario: --intents writes the run in words only, the intent rung: every act its words, for the reasoner each run
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.heart.yaml |
      | --intents      |
      | --format       |
      | yaml           |
    Then artie exits 0
    And artie prints
      | line                                                          |
      | wrote gen.heart.yaml: 0 values to review, 4 reason steps kept |
      | wrote gen.pins.yaml: 0 forms and 0 links pinned               |
    And the file "gen.heart.yaml" reads
      """yaml
      # Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      # The run in words: its shape as it nested, each act said in words for the reasoner to choose on every run.
      # What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      # 4 steps call the model on every run: artie run needs --reasoner.
      #   artie run gen.heart.yaml owner=acme --reasoner claude
      heart: 1
      kind: intent
      start: http://localhost:8392/

      inputs:
        owner:

      steps:
        - intent: open the repository ${owner}
          then:
            - intent: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
              then:
                - sync: true
                - intent: "comment on it: Thanks."
                  then: []
                - intent: close it, since it's done
      """
    And the file "gen.heart.yaml" is a script as data, by spec/schemas/heart-script.draft.schema.json

  Scenario: --intents writes a goal run's watch in words too, from the watch as data, its shape kept
    Given the file "watch.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs:
          owner:
            value: acme
            given: given
            question: Whose repository?
          label:
            value: deps
            given: default
            default: deps
            question: Which label marks a bump?
        source: |-
          act(intent = "open an issue titled \"Merge watch\"")
        marks:
          '1':
            as: watch
            intent: Open an issue titled "Merge watch"
        watch:
          from: 3
          script: |-
            watch(until = { at("watch") { "state" eq "closed" } }) {
                act("github:pulls-list", "owner" to owner, "labels" to label, inferred = "list pull requests of ${owner} labelled ${label}", fromIntent = "a pull request labelled ${label} changes") {
                    whenever {
                        has { "github:labels" has label }
                        once("github:merge", giveUp = 3.minutes) {
                            act("github:merge", "merge_method" to "squash", intent = "merge it by squashing.") {}
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
          steps:
            - watch:
                until:
                  - at: watch
                    field: state
                    is: closed
                steps:
                  - act: github:pulls-list
                    fields:
                      owner: ${owner}
                      labels: ${label}
                    inferred: list pull requests of ${owner} labelled ${label}
                    from-intent: a pull request labelled ${label} changes
                    then:
                      - whenever:
                          - has:
                              - field: github:labels
                                has: ${label}
                          - once:
                              offered: github:merge
                              give-up: 3m
                              steps:
                                - act: github:merge
                                  fields:
                                    merge_method: squash
                                  intent: merge it by squashing.
                                  then: []
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      params:
        entry: https://localhost:8392/
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open an issue titled "Merge watch"
      line: 1
      opens: true
      params:
        relation: github:open-issue
      outcome: new resource
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument         |
      | generate         |
      | watch.trace.yaml |
      | --out            |
      | watch.heart.yaml |
      | --intents        |
      | --format         |
      | yaml             |
    Then artie exits 0
    And the file "watch.heart.yaml" reads
      """yaml
      # Generated by artie generate from watch.trace.yaml.
      # The run in words: its shape as it nested, each act said in words for the reasoner to choose on every run.
      # What it was offered is pinned in watch.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      # 1 step calls the model on every run, and 2 acts in the watch each time one is reached: artie run needs --reasoner.
      #   artie run watch.heart.yaml owner=acme --reasoner claude
      heart: 1
      kind: intent
      start: https://localhost:8392/

      inputs:
        owner:
          question: Whose repository?
        label:
          default: deps
          question: Which label marks a bump?

      steps:
        - intent: Open an issue titled "Merge watch"
          then:
            - keep-as: watch
        - watch:
            until:
              - at: watch
                field: state
                is: closed
            steps:
              - inferred: list pull requests of ${owner} labelled ${label}
                from-intent: a pull request labelled ${label} changes
                then:
                  - whenever:
                      - has:
                          - field: github:labels
                            has: ${label}
                      - once:
                          offered: github:merge
                          give-up: 3m
                          steps:
                            - intent: merge it by squashing.
                              then: []
      """
    And the file "watch.heart.yaml" is a script as data, by spec/schemas/heart-script.draft.schema.json
